🧾 Project Description

This phase extends the previously approved CIB UDL platform implementation to enable the Codify the Bank (CTB) use case to progress towards production by integrating with enterprise knowledge and AI capabilities.

The focus of this phase is to:

* integrate with the on-premise Neo4j enterprise knowledge graph platform
* enable AI model access via the Group AI platform
* support the generation and consumption of structured knowledge from processed documents

This establishes the foundation for CTB to evolve from a document processing capability into an enterprise-aligned knowledge platform.

⸻

🎯 Objectives

* Enable integration with the enterprise Neo4j knowledge graph platform
* Establish AI integration via the Group AI platform for LLM and embedding capabilities
* Support knowledge graph and embedding generation from validated document outputs
* Enable hybrid knowledge representation (graph and vector) for downstream use cases
* Align the solution with enterprise architecture standards for AI and knowledge platforms

⸻

🏗️ Scope

In Scope

1. Knowledge Graph Integration

* Integration with the on-premise Neo4j enterprise platform
* Implementation of knowledge graph build workflows (entity and relationship extraction, transformation, and load)
* Alignment with enterprise ontology and schema models

⸻

2. Group AI Platform Integration

* Integration with the Group AI platform (UDI) for:
    * LLM-based processing (reauthoring and validation)
    * Embedding generation for semantic retrieval

⸻

3. Knowledge Generation

* Enablement of:
    * knowledge graph population from approved content
    * vector embedding generation and storage

⸻

4. Knowledge Retrieval Capability

* Support for:
    * semantic retrieval using embeddings
    * graph-based retrieval from the knowledge graph
    * hybrid retrieval combining graph and vector approaches

⸻

Out of Scope

* Integration with upstream source systems (e.g., GPPS, GMS)
* Automation of ingestion (manual ingestion remains in place)
* Downstream consumer integrations beyond initial platform capability